{title: Come, Thou Long-Expected Jesus}
{artist: Charles Wesley}
{key: F}
{time: 2/4}
{tempo: 84}

Verse 1
[F]Come, thou long-ex[Bb]pected [F]Jesus,
[Dm]born to [Bb]set thy [C]people [F]free;
from our fears and [Bb]sins re[F]lease us,
[Dm]let us [Bb]find our [C]rest in [F]thee.
[Bb]Israel's [F]strength and [C]conso[F]lation,
[Bb]hope of [F]all the [C]earth thou [F]art —
dear de[Bb]sire of [F]every [C]nation,
[Dm]joy of [Bb]every [C]longing [F]heart.

Verse 2
[F]Born Thy people [F]to
[Dm]de liver, [Bb]Born a [C]child [F]and
yet a King, Born [Bb]to reign in
[Dm]us forever, [Bb]Now Thy [C]gracious kingdom [F]bring.
[Bb]By [F]Thine own [C]eternal
[Bb]Spirit Rule [F]in all [C]our hearts [F]alone; By
Thine all sufficient [F]merit, [C]Raise
[Dm]us to [Bb]Thy [C]glorious [F]throne.
